f 17592186045417] [17592186274902 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186274396 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274902 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274902 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274902 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186273392 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274902 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "988def41-f2b9-537a-bb4c-556b664be748" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275088 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186274818 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275088 #edb/ref 1069 "q-143001" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275088 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275088 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/67/67706db50684aef52269d20065caa21e4301834835e10e1fd3e456646ae2b32e.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCDEF$ shown above, which of the following are equal to the vector $\\overset{\\to }{DF}?$\n\nI. $\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BF}$\n\nII. $\\overset{\\to }{FB}-\\overset{\\to }{DB}$\n\nIII. $\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275088 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6378e369-5031-5af4-8366-576c75d82fa3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275088 #edb/ref 1074 "- For the $1$st expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BF} & =(\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB})+\\overset{\\to }{BF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DB}+\\overset{\\to }{BF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DF}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $2$nd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{FB}-\\overset{\\to }{DB} & =\\overset{\\to }{FB}+\\overset{\\to }{BD} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{FD} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{DF}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $3$rd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF} & =\\overset{\\to }{DF}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275206 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186274867 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275206 #edb/ref 1069 "q-149561" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275206 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275206 #edb/ref 1071 "| **Age, in years ($x$)** | $12$ | $12$ | $14$ | $14$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Weight, in lbs ($y$)** | $85$ | $90$ | $97$ | $100$ |\n\nMike plays baseball. The table above shows the ages and corresponding weights of four of Mike's teammates.\nCompute the covariance of the data sets." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275206 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e6f10932-80ef-5d89-b920-551222224129" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275206 #edb/ref 1074 "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x=\\{{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}\\}$ and $y=\\{{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (12+12+14+14) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 52 \\\\  & =13 \\\\ \\overset{―}{y} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (85+90+97+100) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 372 \\\\  & =93\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(12\\,-\\,13)(85\\,-\\,93)+(12\\,-\\,13)(90\\,-\\,93)+(14\\,-\\,13)(97\\,-\\,93)+(14\\,-\\,13)(100\\,-\\,93)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-1)(-8)+(-1)(-3)+(1)(4)+(1)(7)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[8+3+4+7] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 22 \\\\  & =5.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275208 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186274881 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275208 #edb/ref 1069 "q-149570" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275208 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275208 #edb/ref 1071 "| **Years in the 1st division ($x$)** | $44$ | $38$ | $32$ | $30$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Number of Championships ($y$)** | $4$ | $3$ | $3$ | $6$ |\n\nThe table above shows the number of years four English soccer teams have been in the top division and the number of national championships they have won. \nCompute the covariance of the data sets." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275208 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d4368ff5-6ce7-5044-aed6-ebdab8009258" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275208 #edb/ref 1074 "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x=\\{{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}\\}$ and $y=\\{{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (44+38+32+30) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 144 \\\\  & =36 \\\\ \\overset{―}{y} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (4+3+3+6) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 16 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(44\\,-\\,36)(4\\,-\\,4)+(38\\,-\\,36)(3\\,-\\,4)+(32\\,-\\,36)(3\\,-\\,4)+(30\\,-\\,36)(6\\,-\\,4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(8)(0)+(2)(-1)+(-4)(-1)+(-6)(2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[0+(-2)+4+(-12)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-10) \\\\  & =-2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275213 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186274902 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275213 #edb/ref 1069 "q-149616" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275213 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275213 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx=\\{12,\\,7,\\,6,\\,3\\},\\,y=\\{-4,\\,-6,\\,-4,\\,-2\\}\n$$\n\nYou're given that $\\overset{―}{x}=7$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=-4.$ Calculate $\\text{Cov}(x,y).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275213 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "66fe2369-0f88-574b-b368-3759760d7d2e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275213 #edb/ref 1074 "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x=\\{{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}\\}$ and $y=\\{{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(12-7)(-4-(-4))+(7-7)(-6-(-4)) \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,+(6-7)(-4-(-4))+(3-7)(-2-(-4))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(5)(0)+(0)(-2)+(-1)(0)+(-4)(2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[0+0+0-8] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-8) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275214 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186274870 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275214 #edb/ref 1069 "q-149617" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275214 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275214 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx=\\{6,\\,4,\\,8,\\,6\\},\\,y=\\{4,\\,7,\\,11,\\,14\\}\n$$\n\nYou're given that $\\overset{―}{x}=6$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=9.$ Calculate $\\text{Cov}(x,y).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275214 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f9c47870-1c3c-5cbd-a10d-e30d2edb18f8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275214 #edb/ref 1074 "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x=\\{{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}\\}$ and $y=\\{{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(6-6)(4-9)+(4-6)(7-9)+(8-6)(11-9)+(6-6)(14-9)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(0)(-5)+(-2)(-2)+(2)(2)+(0)(5)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[0+4+4+0] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275520 #edb/ref 1080 "images/ba/ba328088ca187ea28b241a302a486da1145a51c7e134d8d4f529f5f4a916ddc1.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275520 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275520 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "049a038d-3516-5ec2-be1b-4e635ba4b278" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275588 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275588 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275588 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0d46a99b-9aed-5723-ae0f-4c64551e3f94" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275674 #edb/ref 1080 "images/ef/efb79fc1071f79597c81a0a974e7f6b21d361ac046f728625e2fe1c02bb507eb.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275674 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275674 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "14ebb756-3759-5271-b48e-6794e5fdec4a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275782 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{3}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275782 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275782 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "21af3edc-3323-554a-bca0-c25456bef3a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276112 #edb/ref 1080 "6" #edb